      "evidence": "Teacher: \"I think the pacing worked well, and next time I would give the quieter students more time to answer.\"",
      "justification": "Teacher names a clear strength (pacing) and a specific area for change (wait-time). The reflection is meaningful but brief and lacks extended justification or multiple examples, so it meets 'some critical identification' rather than deep analysis."
    },
    "connecting_to_incidents": {
      "competency_score": 2,
      "evidence": "Teacher response connects to observed moments of student response variation (early notation-focused answers vs later counting) by attributing the change to pacing.",
      "justification": "Teacher links their observation about pacing to the classroom incidents described in the prompt (opening minutes vs model counting). This shows consistent connection to specific moments, though the example is concise."
    },
    "uptake_of_feedback": {
      "competency_score": 1,
      "evidence": "Teacher: \"...next time I would give the quieter students more time to answer.\"",
      "justification": "Teacher proposes a clear next step but does not reference prior faculty feedback or show evidence of integrating previously given feedback. This indicates limited demonstrated uptake of external faculty suggestions in this short reflection."
    },
    "openness_during_debrief": {
      "competency_score": 2,
      "evidence": "Teacher responded calmly, acknowledged a strength (pacing) and a change to try (wait-time), showing receptive body of thought and willingness to adapt.",
      "justification": "Tone and content indicate openness to change; there was no defensiveness in the brief response."
    }
  }
}
